{"result": {"id": "e10213c6-ea57-4543-8f26-3d64188a4efe", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"ABAP Environment 2508 Overview\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report provides an overview of the key features and updates in the ABAP Environment 2508 release, highlighting the importance of these changes for developers and administrators. The information is relevant to the ABAP Environment 2508 release.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the significant impact of the updates in ABAP Environment 2508 on the development and administration of SAP applications, including improved Fiori-based UIs, enhanced analytics capabilities, and updated security features.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Fiori-Based UI Enhancements\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The ABAP Environment 2508 release introduces several enhancements to Fiori-based UIs, including the ability to expose hierarchical structures as editable treeviews with draft capabilities and the support for server-sent events (SSE). These updates improve the user experience and enable developers to create more interactive and responsive applications. [Data: Sources (1415, 1418), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 14), (2025, 08, 15))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Enhanced Analytics Capabilities\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The ABAP Environment 2508 release includes several updates to enhance analytics capabilities, including the ability to create analytical Fiori applications with real multi-dimensional 'slicing & dicing' capabilities and the support for SQL service and ODBC driver. These updates enable developers to create more advanced analytics applications and improve business decision-making. [Data: Sources (1412, 1416), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 14), (2025, 08, 15))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Security Updates\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The ABAP Environment 2508 release includes several security updates, including the support for server-sent events (SSE) and the ability to display the relevant components for business catalogs and applications. These updates improve the security and reliability of SAP applications and protect against potential threats. [Data: Sources (1418, 1420), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 14), (2025, 08, 15))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2025-02-14\", \"2025-08-15\"]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}}], "created": 1758942871, "model": "gpt-4o", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 506, "prompt_tokens": 10187, "total_tokens": 10693, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "outputTps": 46.550137994480224, "duration": 10.87}}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery.\nInformation discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims.\nThe report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact.\nThe content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their core attributes or capabilities, their connections, and noteworthy claims.\nRetain as much time specific information as possible so your end user can build a timeline of events.\n\n# Report Structure\nThe report should include the following sections:\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title. Avoid including phrases like 'eligibility assessment' or 'eligibility assessment report' in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights.\n- IMPORTANCE RATING: A float score between 0-10 that represents the importance of entities within the community..\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the importance rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n- DATE RANGE: A range of dates (YYYY-MM-DD) with the format [START, END] which corresponds to the date range of text units and intermediate reports used to build the report.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format. Don't use any unnecessary escape sequences. The output should be a single JSON object that can be parsed by json.loads.\n    {\n        \"title\": \"<report_title>\",\n        \"summary\": \"<executive_summary>\",\n        \"rating\": <importance_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": \"<rating_explanation>\",\n        \"findings\": [{\"summary\":\"<insight_1_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_1_explanation\"}, {\"summary\":\"<insight_2_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_2_explanation\"}],\n\t\t\"date_range\": [\"<date range start>\", \"<date range end>\"],\n\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids), <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X resolved a major issue with project Y [Data: Sources (1, 5),  Date_Range ((2001, 05, 12), (2001, 05, 14))]. He also made major updates to the database of app Y [Data: Reports (2, 4), Sources (7, 23, 2, 34, 46, +more), Date_Range ((2001, 05, 15), (2001, 05, 18))\"\"\n\nwhere 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, and 46 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nSOURCES\nid, text\n1, Text: From: compliance.office@enron.com To: management.team@enron.com Cc: legal.team@enron.com, risk@enron.com Date: Wed, 12 Jul 2000 08:30:00 -0600 (CST) Subject: Quick Update on Compliance & Risk Efforts\n2, Quick update on what's been cooking in Compliance and Risk Management. Risk Management is stepping up — They've been tightening up on our financial risk assessments and mitigation strategies since early this year.\n3, Their efforts are key to keeping us on solid ground financially and in compliance with the latest market regulations as of mid-2000. It's crucial for our strategic planning and helps us stay ahead.\n5, Legal's keeping us in check — The Legal Compliance team is on top of ensuring all our operations are up to scratch with legal standards. They're especially focused on improving our corporate governance and contract management as of the second quarter of 2000. This is critical for keeping our operations smooth and legally sound.\n9, Working together — Risk Management and Legal Compliance have been syncing up better than ever since the start of Q2 2000. They're making sure our strategies are not just effective but also fully compliant. This coordination is essential for our integrated governance approach.\n10, Your thoughts? — How do these updates impact your area? Got ideas on how we can do better? Give your department heads a shout.\n11, Thanks for staying engaged. Let's keep pushing for better and smarter ways to work. Cheers, Jane Doe\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n    \"title\": \"Enron Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of July 2000\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report delves into Enron's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2000.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments play in ensuring Enron's adherence to financial and legal regulations, crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Risk Management Operational Scope\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.\n\n[Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Legal Compliance and Governance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices.\n\n[Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Collaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements.\n\n[Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2000-01-01\", \"2000-07-12\"]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----SOURCES-----\nid,text,entity_degree\n101,\"--- Record 1411 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Communication Management: Local APIs\nDescription: The communication management will provide local APIs for the creation and update of communication arrangements, communication systems, communication users, and the upload of client certificates.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1412 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations App: Title Name Change\nDescription: When a business configuration object is selected, the application title now changes to the name of the business configuration object.See Custom Business Configurations App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1413 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Integration Using SQL Service\nDescription: The documentation Accessing ABAP-Managed Data Using SQL Services for Data Integration Scenarios has moved to a central guide dedicated to integration and connectivity. You can find all information relating to accessing ABAP-managed data using SQL services in the chapters about data integration: ABAP Integration and Connectivity: Data Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1414 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Developing Inbound and Outbound Communication\nDescription: The documentation Developing External Service Consumption (Outbound Communication) and Developing APIs for Inbound Communication has been moved to a central guide dedicated to integration and connectivity. You can find all information relating to inbound and outbound communication in the chapters about process integration: ABAP Integration and Connectivity: Process Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1415 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Editable Treeview with Draft Capabilities\nDescription: In RAP, a treeview visualizes data modeled by a CDS hierarchy, using an SAP Fiori Elements treetable. Previously, you could model hierarchical structures and expose them as read-only treeviews to the SAP Fiori UI. Now you can also expose hierarchical structures as editable treeviews with draft capabilities.   For more information, see Treeviews and Editable Treeviews with Draft Capabilities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1416 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Event-Driven Side Effects\nDescription: You can now define an event to trigger a side effect in your RAP business object. Whenever a defined event is raised by the application server, the side effect is triggered and the defined targets are reloaded.   For more information, see Event-Driven RAP Side Effects\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1417 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Export Customizing Transports: Release All\nDescription: You can now release all open customizing requests at once.See Working in the Export Customizing Transports App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1418 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Harmonized Context Menu in Key User Adaptation\nDescription: The context menu is now consistent when you select elements. It no longer depends on how you select an element, such as using the left or right mouse button. The familiar right-click context menu now also appears when you left-click an element.  For more information, see Making UI Changes (Object Pages).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1419 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hide Empty Spaces and Pages in the SAP Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: Spaces and pages are not shown when they are empty because of the user's role context. This feature is opt-in, so it's disabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES  is set to the default value false that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Note  SAP plans to activate this feature by default with the upcoming 2505 SAP BTP ABAP environment release. You can now try it out and inform your users, if necessary, about a potential change of behavior.With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from\",976\n664,\"2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 848 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Archiving: Storage Manager Implementation\nDescription: You can now use a new interface method to rollback faulty verified archive files.See Storage Manager Implementation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 849 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hide Empty Spaces and Pages in the SAP Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: Spaces and pages are not shown when they are empty because of the user's role context. This feature is now enabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES is set to the default value true that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from the Manage Launchpad Settings app, and empty spaces and pages will continue to be hidden by default.  For more information, see Empty Spaces and Pages Not Displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-14\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 850 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: IAM Information System\nDescription: You can now display the relevant components for business catalogs and applications. This way you can check under which component you can create an incident if required.For more information, see IAM Information System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n\",846\n102,\" feature is opt-in, so it's disabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES  is set to the default value false that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Note  SAP plans to activate this feature by default with the upcoming 2505 SAP BTP ABAP environment release. You can now try it out and inform your users, if necessary, about a potential change of behavior.With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from the Manage Launchpad Settings app, and empty spaces and pages will continue to be hidden by default.  For more information, see Empty Spaces and Pages Not Displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1420 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: How to Display Open Transport Requests\nDescription: You can now display open transport requests by searching a table in the Manage Software Components app.  For more information, see Display Open Transport Requests.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n\",616\n151,\"--- Record 271 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Fiori UIs for Communication Management Change History\nDescription: It is now possible to view the communication management change history in Fiori UIs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 272 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Fiori-Based Multi-Dimensional Reporting – Cloud-Compliant\nDescription: You need to quickly build an analytical Fiori application, but simple list reporting doesn’t satisfy your needs? Instead, you already built an analytical model with the new embedded analytics capabilities of the developer extensibility and now want to unleash its full potential? In that case, we have the right solution for you: Without writing a single line of additional code, you can simply expose your model in a full-fledged analytical application with a modern Fiori-based UI and real multi-dimensional “slicing & dicing” capabilities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 273 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Fiori-Based Multi-Report Applications\nDescription: You need to quickly build an analytical Fiori application, that puts multiple analytical queries into one context in a single UI?  All you need to do is to provide the queries, bundle them in an InA Service and you are good to just start the brand new \"\"Review Booklet Application\"\" wizard to generate the application. Afterwards, you can refine the configuration of your Review Booklet in an easy to use Fiori UI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 274 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Generation Wizard: Outbound SQL via CDS External Entities\nDescription: The ADT generation wizard allows you to develop outbound SQL scenarios more efficiently by generating the required CDS external entities based on an imported CSN definition of the remote SQL API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 275 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Grouping Events as Activities\nDescription: With this release, events of the same type and object occurring in the same session are grouped as activities. Sequences in the application Display Business Events by Objects are displayed according to activities. A new CDS view is also released to retrieve activity details.  An activity is an action performed by a user or the system that initiates an event in the system.  For more information, see Display Business Events by Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 276 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hidden Empty Spaces and Pages in the SAP Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: Spaces and pages are not shown when they are empty because of the user's role context. Empty spaces and pages will be hidden by default.  For more information, see Empty Spaces and Pages Not Displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 277 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Log RAP-based C1 events\nDescription: This feature enables the logging of C1-released, RAP-based events for local consumption.  For more information, see Display Business Event Logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 278 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Manage Security Audit Log (F6996A)\nDescription: This app is the successor of the F6996 app. The F6996 app is deprecated and will be deleted from the SAP Fiori launchpad in an upcoming release. The deprecated app may no longer be available by default on the SAP Fiori launchpad. In this case, you can find it in the app finder until it is deleted. We recommend that you switch to the successor app as soon as possible.  See Manage Security Audit Log.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 279 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Manage Software Components\nDescription: The delete dialog for Bring Your Own Git has been modified. The Unregister repository checkbox within the dialog has been moved outside the dialog and changed to a separate\",497\n488,\"--- Record 2631 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: HTML5 Business Solution as a Content Provider\nDescription: It is now possible to create an HTML5 business solution that behaves as a content provider in the subaccount.  The HTML5 business solution can be consumed by the local subaccount and also by other subaccounts that access it via destinations.  To configure the HTML5 busines solution as a content provider, the following actions are required:   Provider subaccount: the HTML5 code should be adjusted and include a cdm.json file that defines the design-time business content (for example, roles, groups, spaces & pages), and destinations.    Consumer subaccount: it is required to configure destinations that will point to the HTML5 business solution and create the content provider.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2632 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sort Order of Spaces\nDescription: In sites that are using Spaces and Pages - New Experience display mode, spaces are sorted in the menu at runtime as follows:    Content channel: spaces from the same content channel will appear next to each other in the menu       Local spaces are displayed first    Content channels are sorted by their ID      Sort priority: spaces from the same content channel are sorted according to their “Sort Priority”, from low to high    Sort priorities are either defined in the content channel or locally for local spaces (a new UI control is now available).    When no sort priority is defined, the default value is set to zero.      Title: when the content channel and sort priority is the same  ID when the content channel, sort priority, and title are the same   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2633 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Update Operation in Identity Provisioning Transformation\nDescription: The default target transformation code of an SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition system in the Identity Provisioning service, has been enhanced to also support updates to existing user records. With this enhancement, when a user attribute changes (for example email address or Global ID), the record is updated instead of being skipped.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-11\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: 2406B\n\n--- Record 2634 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.98.1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.97.0 to 1.98.1. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 9 is updated from version 9.0.89 to 9.0.90      SpotBugs is updated from version 4.8.5 to 4.8.6      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.20.17 to 2.21.10      com.sap.cloud.connectivity.apiext is updated from version 3.35.0 to 3.36.0      com.sap.conn.jco-cloud is updated from version 3.1.9.0 to 3.1.10.0      com.sap.xs.onpremise.runtime is updated from version 1.2.2 to 1.2.3    JVM option \"\"-XX:+UseContainerCpuShares\"\" is now replaced by \"\"-XX:ActiveProcessorCount=<value>\"\". It prevents out-of-memory errors in case a GC algorithm with high internal memory usage has been activated in small containers (< 4GB). See: ActiveProcessorCount  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2635 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.12.1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.11.0 to 2.12.1. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.24 to 10.1.25      SpotBugs is updated from version 4.8.5 to 4.8.6      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.20.17 to 2.21.10      com.sap.cloud.connectivity.apiext is updated from version 3.35.0 to 3.36.0      com.sap.conn.jco-cloud is updated from version 3.1.9.0 to 3.1.10.0      com.sap.xs.onpremise.runtime is updated from version 1.2.2 to 1.2.3    JVM option \"\"-XX:+UseContainerCpuShares\"\" is now replaced by \"\"-XX:ActiveProcessorCount=<value>\"\". It prevents out-of-memory errors in case a GC algorithm with high internal memory usage has been activated in small containers (< 4GB). See: ActiveProcessorCount  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine\",433\n219,\"--- Record 2451 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Applications in the ABAP Environment: Scoping Space and Page Templates\nDescription: You can now assign space and page templates to a business role template. Furthermore, a default scope for space and page templates is set automatically in test and production systems, depending on the software component.   For more information, see Working with Business Role Template Launchpad Space Template Assignmens and Scoping Space and Page Templates.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2452 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Define the Home Title in the Shell Bar\nDescription: You can now specify an alternative text for the Home text in the shell bar. This is an optional alternative title for the shell and browser tab when navigating to the starting pages. The default value is empty, which means \"\"Home\"\" (or the respective translation) is used.   For more information, see Manage Launchpad Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2453 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Define the Launchpad Title in the Browser\nDescription: In the SAP Fiori launchpad, you can now adjust the title shown as the window, and the tab title in the browser, according to your needs. In the Manage Launchpad Settings app, the new parameter WINDOW_TITLE_EXTENSION was added. With this parameter, administrators can specify an additional text following \"\"Home\"\", or the app title. Text translations can be added if required. The text will also be interpreted by a screenreader to enhance usability and accessibility.  For more information, see Manage Launchpad Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2454 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Upload and Download Pages\nDescription: In the Manage Launchpad Pages app, you can now select and download existing pages or upload pages that were downloaded in another system. This enables you to create backups or exchange pages between different systems when you can't use transports, meaning that you can improve productivity across different systems. This also saves you time and effort because you don't need to recreate everything from scratch.  For more information, see Uploading and Downloading Pages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2455 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Selectable Application Server Sizes\nDescription: The selectable application server size feature gives you the possibility to explicitly configure either 0.5 ACUs or 2 ACUs as the size of the application servers. With this feature, it's now possible to configure application servers of size 2 ACUs for an SAP BTP ABAP environment system that uses the elastic scaling feature.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2456 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SQL Service and ODBC Driver\nDescription: With the new system views SYS.FUNCTIONS and SYS.FUNCTION_PARAMETERS, you can find automatically exposed CDS SQL-based scalar functions and retrieve their metadata. You can use these CDS SQL-based scalar functions to get ABAP-based data using the SQL service and the ODBC driver.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2457 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Technical Monitoring: HANA Thread Samples\nDescription: With the new HANA Thread Samples app, you can check how much HANA CPU time your custom applications consume. The app helps you to identify your top workload that consumes most of the HANA CPU time, from where you can drill down to a detailed view of HANA thread samples and the related single SQL statements.  See HANA Thread Samples\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-12\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2458 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Technical Monitoring: Table Analysis\nDescription: The Table Analysis app has been enhanced with more information about top column tables by growth, writes, reads, and writes and about top column indexes by size. The monitoring screens Top Column Tables by Growth, Top Column Tables by Reads, Top Column Tables by Writes, Top Column Indexes by Size, and Top\",343\n184,\"--- Record 41 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.40.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.39.0 to 2.40.0. Updated components:       Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.44 to 10.1.45      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 5.0.1 to 5.0.2      com.sap.cloud.security.xsuaa is updated from version 3.6.3 to 3.6.4    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-20\nValid as Of: 2025-10-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 42 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Administrator's Guide\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: Updated Shared Responsibility Model\nDescription: In alignment with the learning journey for administrators, we've updated the Shared Responsibility Model Between You and SAP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-25\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 43 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Content Displayed on SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: We’ve corrected the unintended behavior of content in the different view modes of Groups and Spaces and Pages when using SAP Mobile Start.   Now when accessing a site on SAP Mobile Start, only the content that is relevant to the selected view mode is displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: 2509A\n\n--- Record 44 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Content Displayed on SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: We’ve corrected the unintended behavior of content in the different view modes of Groups and Spaces and Pages when using SAP Mobile Start.   Now when accessing a site on SAP Mobile Start, only the content that is relevant to the selected view mode is displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-29\nVersion: 2509A\n\n--- Record 45 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New Type of User for Agent Registration\nDescription: For increased security, you now use a new type of user called an Agent user to register a Data Services Agent. For more information, see User Administration and Registering an Agent in the Web Interface.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-08\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 46 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: \"\"DSOD\"\" No Longer Appears in the URL for SAP Cloud Integration for data services\nDescription: \"\"DSOD\"\" has been removed from the URL for SAP Cloud Integration for data services on SAP BTP, Kyma runtime. The following documentation has been modified:  Finish Setting Up a Standard User  Creating a Client to Use Web Services  Accessing the WSDL File  Agent Diagnostics Available via the Command Line  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 47 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Announcement: User Interface Supporting Migration from the Neo Environment to Kyma Runtime\nDescription: In the Administration user interface of SAP Cloud Integration for data services, an Off-Neo Migration workflow is being rolled out. Once enabled for you, the workflow guides you through the process of migrating from the Neo environment to the Kyma runtime. You will receive an SAP Customer Communication with details about the availability of this workflow in your system. The Tenant Migration Guide and in particular UI Location and Visibility of the Tenant Migration Request contain helpful information about the workflow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 48 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Compilation of Security Recommendations\nDescription: Security-related recommendations that appear in various places within the SAP Cloud Integration for data services documentation set have been compiled into an easily readable table in Security Recommendations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 49 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Do Not Use Standard Users for Web Services\nDescription: User Administration has been updated to reflect that standard users should not be used for web services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\",309\n367,\"Type: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 287 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.136.4 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2025 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 288 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Manage Launchpad Spaces and Pages: Redesign and Renaming\nDescription: In the SAP Fiori launchpad, both the Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages apps were redesigned. We adapted the overview pages to enhance working with spaces and space templates, as well as with pages and page templates. \"\"Predefined\"\" and \"\"SAP-Delivered\"\" were renamed to \"\"Templates\"\" to ensure consistent terminology between these apps, the Maintain Business Roles app and the ABAP Development Tools for space and page templates.  See Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 289 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: New Layout for Launchpad Shell Bar and Menus\nDescription: The layout of the SAP Fiori launchpad shell bar, user menu, notifications list, navigation menu and user settings was changed according to the current SAP Design System. The user experience was harmonized across different SAP products. The navigation menu was enhanced and is now part of the shell bar. It now offers access to My Home, Favorite Apps, My Spaces and All Spaces.   The sorting options in the notifications list were simplified. In addition, there is a new button to directly open the settings from here. The order of entries in the user menu as well as in the user settings has been adapted.  See User Menu, Shell and Shell Bar and Working with Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 290 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Server-Sent Events in ABAP HTTP\nDescription: The ABAP HTTP client and server now support server-sent events (SSE). Which allows a server to send parts of the body of the response to the client without the client having to actively request them. After being sent by the server, the client can fetch them as they become available.  For more information, see Enabling Server-Sent Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n\",309\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_5f69506b3a1052ebbabffb7e5ae4d10fbcc2aec856863134cc5b4a6b06625a63_v2"}